# Project Structure

## Directory Organization
- Keep related files together in feature folders
- Use clear, descriptive folder names
- Follow the established feature-based architecture
- Keep shared components in the `shared` directory
- Maintain consistent directory structure across features

## File Organization
- One widget per file
- Keep files focused and single-purpose
- Use appropriate file extensions (`.dart`, `.mdc`, etc.)
- Group related files in feature folders
- Follow the established naming conventions

## Feature Structure
Each feature should follow this structure:
```
feature_name/
├── models/         # Data models and entities
├── providers/      # State management
├── widgets/        # UI components
├── screens/        # Full screens/pages
└── services/       # Business logic
```

## Shared Resources
- Place shared widgets in `shared/widgets`
- Put common utilities in `shared/utils`
- Store constants in `shared/constants`
- Keep theme-related code in `shared/theme`
- Place shared services in `shared/services`

## Asset Organization
```
assets/
├── images/         # App images and icons
├── fonts/          # Custom fonts
└── icons/          # App icons
```

## Naming Conventions
- Use lowercase with underscores for directory names
- Prefix feature-specific directories with feature name
- Use clear, descriptive names for all directories
- Follow the established directory hierarchy
- Keep directory names consistent with their purpose
